Vercel is auto-detecting Python instead of treating it as a static site. The fix is to explicitly tell Vercel "this is a static site, no framework, no build".
📁 Updated vercel.json — Explicit Static Site
{
  "version": 2,
  "public": true,
  "framework": null,
  "buildCommand": null,
  "installCommand": null,
  "outputDirectory": ".",
  "cleanUrls": true,
  "trailingSlash": false,
  "rewrites": [
    { "source": "/checkout", "destination": "/checkout.html" },
    { "source": "/checkout/payment/success", "destination": "/checkout.html" },
    { "source": "/checkout/payment/error", "destination": "/checkout.html" },
    { "source": "/checkout/payment/cancelled", "destination": "/checkout.html" },
    { "source": "/", "destination": "/checkout.html" }
  ],
  "headers": [
    {
      "source": "/(.*)",
      "headers": [
        { "key": "X-Content-Type-Options", "value": "nosniff" },
        { "key": "X-Frame-Options", "value": "DENY" },
        { "key": "Referrer-Policy", "value": "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" },
        { "key": "Permissions-Policy", "value": "geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()" },
        { "key": "Strict-Transport-Security", "value": "max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
📁 Updated package.json — Explicit Static
{
  "name": "checkout-billing-payflow-buzz",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "PayFlow Billing Checkout — billing.payflow.buzz",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {
    "build": "exit 0"
  }
}
🔑 Key changes that fix the error:
| Setting | Before | After | Why | |---|---|---|---| | "framework" | (not set) | null | Tells Vercel: no framework, don't auto-detect Python/Next/etc | | "buildCommand" | null | null | No build step | | "installCommand" | (not set) | null | Don't install anything (no node_modules, no pip) | | "build" script | echo '...' | exit 0 | Clean exit, no output |
📁 Final structure — exactly 3 files, nothing else:
checkout-billing.payflow.buzz/
├── package.json
├── vercel.json
└── checkout.html
Important: Make sure there are no other files in the repo — no main.py, no requirements.txt, no runtime.txt. If any Python file exists in the repo, delete it. Vercel sees a .py file and assumes Python project.
Push and redeploy — Vercel will now serve checkout.html as a static site. ✅
